  "_comment": "Negative, and the one that proves the disabling holds at DEPTH rather than at a fixed number of hops. The finding cites one proof record, that proof record's rkaf:proofSupportingRecord names a second, entirely legitimate, assertion-state proof, and only THAT one names the closure claim. Every hop on the chain is a legal edge carrying a legal proof type, so nothing per-property objects; an earlier four-branch one-hop form of rkaf:ClosureClaimNotFindingEvidenceShape let this document validate, which meant omission could be enabled by interposing one extra proof record. Caught by rkaf:ClosureClaimNotFindingEvidenceShape (spec/rkaf-analysis.md 6.4 mechanism 3). This is one of only two fixtures permitted to contain a ClosureClaim and a RelationFinding together, and it must fail."
